    {
      "month": "1981-04",
      "title": "The first space shuttle launches",
      "description": "Columbia carries two astronauts into orbit on the first shuttle mission. The flight opens a new chapter in US space travel.",
      "source_ids": ["nasa-sts1"]
    },
    {
      "month": "1981-08",
      "title": "IBM introduces its personal computer",
      "description": "IBM launches a computer aimed at businesses and homes. It uses components and software from outside suppliers.",
      "source_ids": ["ibm-pc-history"]
    },
    {
      "month": "1982-11",
      "title": "The recession reaches a turning point",
      "description": "Economic activity reaches the low point later identified by the NBER. Its official announcement follows in July 1983.",
      "source_ids": ["nber-1982-trough"]
    }
  ],
  "what_happened_next": {
    "text": "High inflation was followed by another recession, then recovery. All seven choices ended higher after five years, but their gains differed greatly. IBM finished first in this set; Texas Instruments finished last. A promising industry did not make every company an equally rewarding investment. These dollar gains also do not tell you how much prices rose while you waited.",
