      "fed-1981-recession"
    ]
  },
  "reflection": {
    "what_people_were_focused_on": "People worried about rising prices, expensive borrowing and another recession. Computers and medical research offered exciting possibilities.",
    "what_actually_mattered": "The seven return paths mattered more than one dramatic headline. Interest and dividends added to returns, and each company faced its own risks.",
    "what_faded_away": "Campaign tactics and excitement about breakfast cereals did not tell you which investment would lead five years later.",
    "what_nobody_knew": "The exact turns in the economy and the ranking of these choices were unknown. High starting interest rates did not make the next five years easy to predict.",
